<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>2.2.1.2 Table of Values and Graph of function</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p class="tb-exercise">Exercise</p>
<p>Complete the table of values for the function \( f(x) = {@f@} \) for \(x\) between \(-3\) and \(3\).</p>
<table class="tb-table">
<tbody>
<tr><th style="text-align:left;">input, \(x\)</th><th style="text-align:left;">output, \(f(x)\)</th></tr>
<tr><td style="text-align:left;">\(-3\)</td><td style="text-align:left;">\({@fatneg3@}\)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="text-align:left;">\(-2\)</td><td style="text-align:left;">\({@fatneg2@}\)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="text-align:left;">\(-1\)</td><td style="text-align:left;">[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</td></tr>
<tr><td style="text-align:left;">\(0\)</td><td style="text-align:left;">[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</td></tr>
<tr><td style="text-align:left;">\(1\)</td><td style="text-align:left;">[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</td></tr>
<tr><td style="text-align:left;">\(2\)</td><td style="text-align:left;">[[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt5]]</td></tr>
<tr><td style="text-align:left;">\(3\)</td><td style="text-align:left;">\({@fat3@}\)</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Using your table of values, which graph shows the function \( f(x) = {@f@} \)?</p>
<table>
<tbody>
<tr><td style="text-align:center;"><b>Graph A</b></td><td style="text-align:center;"><b>Graph B</b></td></tr>
<tr><td style="text-align:center;">{@thumbnailplot(funcstoplot[1],"Graph A")@}</td><td style="text-align:center;">{@thumbnailplot(funcstoplot[2],"Graph B")@}</td></tr>
<tr><td style="text-align:center;"><b>Graph C</b></td><td style="text-align:center;"><b>Graph D</b></td></tr>
<tr><td style="text-align:center;">{@thumbnailplot(funcstoplot[3],"Graph C")@}</td><td style="text-align:center;">{@thumbnailplot(funcstoplot[4],"Graph D")@}</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<div>Graph [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>To complete a table of values, substitute each input \(x\) into the rule \(f(x) = {@f@}\). Remember that cubing a negative number gives a negative number, because \((-1)^3 = (-1)(-1)(-1) = -1\).</p>
<p>\(f(-1) = {@a@}(-1)^3 = {@ta2@}\),</p>
<p>\(f(0) = {@a@}(0)^3 = {@ta3@}\),</p>
<p>\(f(1) = {@a@}(1)^3 = {@ta4@}\),</p>
<p>\(f(2) = {@a@}(2)^3 = {@a@} \times 8 = {@ta5@}\).</p>
<p>The function \(f(x) = {@f@}\) is a <strong>cubic function</strong>: the highest power of \(x\) is 3. Because the coefficient \({@a@}\) is positive, its graph rises from the bottom left to the top right. It passes through the origin, where it flattens out and changes the way it bends (a point of inflection), giving the typical S-shape. Plotting the points from the table, such as \((-1, {@ta2@})\), \((0, 0)\) and \((1, {@ta4@})\), and comparing them with the four graphs identifies the right one: Graph {@first(mcq_correct(ta1))@}.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
